        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"title\": \"[QA Failure Handoff] Playwright Test Run #{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.run_number }} Failed (Branch: {{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.ref }})\",\n  \"body\": \"### 🚨 Automated QA Failure Report\\n\\n**Correlation ID:** `{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.correlation_id }}`\\n**Repository:** `{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.repo_owner }}/{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.repo_name }}`\\n**Commit SHA:** `{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.head_sha }}`\\n**GitHub Run:** [View GitHub Actions Run #{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.run_number }}]({{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.html_url }})\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🖥️ Secure Antigravity Desktop / Local Handoff Instructions\\n*n8n Cloud cannot connect directly to localhost. Follow these steps to reproduce and triage locally:*\\n\\n1. **Checkout the exact failing commit:**\\n   ```bash\\n   git fetch origin\\n   git checkout {{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.head_sha }}\\n   ```\\n2. **Inspect Artifacts & Traces:**\\n   Download the Playwright trace archive from GitHub Actions Run #{{ $('Verify Conclusion & SHA').item.json.run_number }}.\\n3. **Local Fix & Push:**\\n   Fix the issue and commit to trigger the next validation run.\",\n  \"labels\": [\"qa-failure\", \"automated-triage\"]\n}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 15000
        }
      },
